Z||000000||Greg Piet||10-07-1999||12:08 AM||||Are there any hardcore racers out there with fiero's?  A friend jokingly said as i was discussing putting a turbo in my fiero, "What are you going to do drive the cannonball?"<BR>That sparked my interest, so I went wandering around looking to see if the cannonball was still around or if it was killed by some killjoy. I am curious if anyone out here in fieroland has thought of running the new cannonball now called the lap of america?  Also curious what peoples comments are on this(If you want to pick on me feel free I can take it).  Call me toatally insane, but a beefed up Fiero might be able to hold its own.||||reg||1
Z||000001||ChadMan||10-07-1999||08:49 AM||||A souped-up Fiero could definitely hold its own in the One Lap competition!  I subscribe to C/D and I want to think a hopped-up Plymouth Valiant finished in the top 10 a couple of years ago.  They have some racetrack events where the Vipers and Vettes would stomp you, but I think most of One Lap is a timed road rally that wouldn't reward out-and-out speed.<P>Tip for long-distance Fiero travelers:  Pick a short traveling companion.  Then you can stash snack foods, atlases, and one of those long, thin can coolers behind the passenger seat!||||reg||1
